    "font" : null,
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "content" : "1. INTRODUCTION"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 41,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 83.0, 183.667, 529.333, 317.667 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Cluster algebras. Cluster algebras were introduced by Fomin and Zelevinsky [FZ02] as a combinatorial approach to the upper global bases of quantum groups and to the theory of total positivity in algebraic groups. A cluster algebra of rank n (with trivial coeﬃcients) is a Z -subalgebra of a rational function ﬁeld generated by a special set of generators called cluster variables , which are grouped into overlapping subsets of ﬁxed size n , called clusters . A seed t = ( x t ,B t ) is a pair consisting of a cluster x t = ( x 1; t ,...,x n ; t ) and a skew-symmetrizable integer matrix B t = ( b t ij ) n × n , called an exchange matrix . One can obtain new seeds from a given one by a procedure called mutation . The sets of cluster variables and clusters of a cluster algebra are determined by an initial seed and the iterative mutations. A cluster momomial is a monomial in variables from the same cluster. The remarkable Laurent phenomenon [FZ02] says that the expansion of a cluster monomial u with repect to any cluster x t is a Laurent polynomial."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 42,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 83.667, 123.667, 528.0, 185.0 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "The notions of g -vectors and F -polynomials associated to cluster monomials are introduced in [FZ07]. To each cluster monomial u and any initial seed t = ( x t ,B t ), one has the g -vector g t u ∈ Z n and F -polynomial F t u ( y 1 ,...,y n ) ∈ Z [ y 1 ,...,y n ] with respect to seed t = ( x t ,B t ). It is known from [GHKK18] that the F -polynomial F t u has non-negative coeﬃcients and constant term 1. Fomin and Zelevinsky [FZ07] proved that the Laurent expansion of u with respect to seed t can be written as:"
  }, {
    "type" : "formula",
    "pdfua_tag" : "Formula",
    "id" : 43,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 84.333, 104.333, 107.0, 117.0 ],
    "content" : "(1.1)"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 44,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 83.333, 75.0, 528.333, 99.667 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "where ˆ y k ; t = x B t e k t and e k is the k th column of I n . We call (1.1) the canonical expression of u with respect to seed t ."
